{
  "requirement": "The SDK derives the submission tool's JSON schema from `R` using `schemars`\nand instructs the agent to finish through that tool. Its default name is\n`submit_result`; harness configuration can preserve an application's existing\nnames and acceptance rules.\n\nA successful call returns exactly one accepted submitted value, deserialized\ninto `R`. Ordinary assistant text does not count. Ending without a valid\naccepted submission returns an error. Provider failures and invalid terminal\nsubmissions return `ValidationError::Agent`, rather than a node judgment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.submission`.\n\n- **Schema from `R`, default name, and instruction to finish through the tool.**\n  - `tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` finds the `submit_result` tool in the request. It asserts the schema's `result` type is `boolean` for `R = bool`.\n  - `tests/agent.rs#fn[typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors]` does the same for a structured `Answer`. It asserts that `$defs.Decision` exists and that the `decision` property is a `$ref` into it.\n  - `tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts the schema passed to the mock agent has `n` of type `integer`. The `MockAgent` in `tests/validation.rs` asserts `submission_name == \"submit_result\"`.\n  - `tests/agent.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` asserts the prompt contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\".\n- **A successful call returns the accepted value deserialized into `R`.** The `bool` case returns `true`, the `Answer` case returns `Decision::Yes`, and the mock-agent test returns `n == 7`. `tests/agent.rs#fn[unknown_tools_return_errors_without_creating_inputs_or_preventing_submission]` shows an unknown tool call does not stop a later valid submission.\n- **Ordinary assistant text does not count, and ending without an accepted submission is an error.** `tests/agent.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` uses a text-only provider. It asserts `ValidationError::Agent` with the message \"without invoking submit_result\".\n- **Exactly one accepted submission.** `tests/agent.rs#fn[typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors]` loops over three bad cases and asserts `ValidationError::Agent` for each:\n  - a wrong-typed result;\n  - two submissions in one turn;\n  - an extra top-level field.\n- **Provider failures and invalid terminal submissions return `ValidationError::Agent`, not a node judgment.** `tests/agent.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` asserts this for a permanent provider failure. It also asserts that no dependencies are recorded. `tests/validation.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` asserts it for an invalid typed submission from the mock agent.\n- **Configurable names and acceptance rules.** The text says only that harness configuration \"can\" preserve an application's names and rules. That is permissive, not a MUST or SHOULD, so it creates no testing obligation here. The default behavior it contrasts with is tested.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept. The tests assert on outcomes and schema content, not just on execution.",
  "references": "1650f360ea3553ba682752a3e45209439ee8f09a3433c586c8255959404d47d1",
